+Please generate cardiac organoids from human induced pluripotent stem cells using the previously published protocol by Hofbauer et al. Maintain them at 37 °C in 95% air and 5% CO2 in chemically defined medium (CDM) prepared from a 1:1 mix of IMDM and F-12 Nutrient Mix, supplemented with 5 mg/mL BSA, 1% chemically defined concentrated lipids, 0.004% 1-thiolglycerol, 15 µg/mL transferrin, 10 µg/mL insulin, and 100 mg/mL VEGF-165. Reassociate the organoids into Corning 96-well black/clear round-bottom ultra-low attachment spheroid microplates at day 0. Perform size measurements of the organoid diameter using brightfield imaging via the Leica Application Suite microscope software.
 
